          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 47.64,
          "end": 50.1,
          "en": "to listen to our providers",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 50.1,
          "end": 52.98,
          "en": "and to changes in those provider values.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 52.98,
          "end": 56.07,
          "en": "Now if we did not have a stateful widget here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 56.07,
          "end": 59.34,
          "en": "but a stateless widget, we would replace this",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 59.34,
          "end": 62.76,
          "en": "with ConsumerWidget like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 62.76,
          "end": 64.98,
          "en": "But since we had a stateful widget here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 64.98,
          "end": 69.15,
          "en": "it's ConsumerStatefulWidget, which we'll need to use.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 69.15,
          "end": 72.84,
          "en": "But we'll see consumer widget in action later as well.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 72.84,
          "end": 76.71000000000001,
          "en": "Now with the widget class extending ConsumerStatefulWidget,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 76.71000000000001,
          "end": 79.2,
          "en": "we also have to change the state class",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 79.2,
          "end": 81.33,
          "en": "also to get rid of this error here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 81.33,
          "end": 84.75,
          "en": "and here, we now have to extend ConsumerState",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 84.75,
          "end": 86.283,
          "en": "instead of just state.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 87.33,
          "end": 90.09,
          "en": "In addition, we should also use ConsumerState",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 90.09,
          "end": 91.413,
          "en": "as a type here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 92.31,
          "end": 94.17,
          "en": "So now we got rid of all these errors,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 94.17,
          "end": 96.96000000000001,
          "en": "and we're extending these consumer classes",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 96.96000000000001,
          "end": 99.72,
          "en": "for both the widget class and the state class.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 99.72,
          "end": 103.65,
          "en": "Now by doing so, we behind the scenes add functionality",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 103.65,
          "end": 105.99000000000001,
          "en": "to those classes that allows us",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 105.99000000000001,
          "end": 109.44,
          "en": "to reach out to the providers we might have defined",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 109.44,
          "end": 111.093,
          "en": "like this meals provider here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 112.17,
          "end": 114.47999999999999,
          "en": "And we can use this functionality here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 114.47999999999999,
          "end": 116.793,
          "en": "in the TabsScreenState class now.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 117.63,
          "end": 120.12,
          "en": "There I want to get my meals,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 120.12,
          "end": 123.66,
          "en": "and previously here I imported and used dummy meals.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 123.66,
          "end": 126.75,
          "en": "Now we can get those meals from the provider.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 126.75,
          "end": 127.583,
          "en": "And for that,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 127.583,
          "end": 130.92,
          "en": "we've now got a new ref property available here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 130.92,
          "end": 132.78,
          "en": "in this state class.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 132.78,
          "end": 134.64,
          "en": "Just as we have widget available",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 134.64,
          "end": 138.21,
          "en": "to reach out to the widget that belongs to this state,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 138.21,
          "end": 140.73,
          "en": "we now have a ref property available",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 140.73,
          "end": 144.84,
          "en": "that allows us to set up listeners to our providers.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 144.84,
          "end": 147.87,
          "en": "So this ref property is added by Riverpod,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 147.87,
          "end": 149.25,
          "en": "and it is available",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 149.25,
          "end": 152.76,
          "en": "because we are extending consumer state here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 152.76,
          "end": 154.143,
          "en": "in this state class.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 155.07,
          "end": 157.8,
          "en": "Now with this ref property available,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 157.8,
          "end": 160.98,
          "en": "the question of course is what we can do with it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 160.98,
          "end": 162.27,
          "en": "And what we can do",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 162.27,
          "end": 164.94,
          "en": "is we can use a couple of utility methods.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 164.94,
          "end": 169.94,
          "en": "Most importantly read to get data from our provider once",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 170.37,
          "end": 172.82999999999998,
          "en": "or watch to set up a listener",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 172.82999999999998,
          "end": 175.92000000000002,
          "en": "that will make sure that the build method executes again",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 175.92000000000002,
          "end": 178.26,
          "en": "as our data changes.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 178.26,
          "end": 181.2,
          "en": "And the official Riverpod documentation",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 181.2,
          "end": 184.23,
          "en": "recommends to use watch as often as possible,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 184.23,
          "end": 187.35,
          "en": "even if you technically only need to read data once,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 187.35,
          "end": 190.41,
          "en": "because this way if you ever change your logic,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 190.41,
          "end": 192.78,
          "en": "you can't run into unintended bugs",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 192.78,
          "end": 196.23,
          "en": "where you forget to replace a read with a watch.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 196.23,
          "end": 197.73,
          "en": "That's why they recommend",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 197.73,
          "end": 201.12,
          "en": "that you always use watch right from the start.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 201.12,
          "end": 204.39,
          "en": "Now watch needs a parameter though,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 204.39,
          "end": 208.23,
          "en": "and the parameter it needs or the argument it needs",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 208.23,
          "end": 210.09,
          "en": "is a provider.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 210.09,
          "end": 213.32999999999998,
          "en": "So here we now wanna use the meals provider",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 213.32999999999998,
          "end": 217.35,
          "en": "that we created and stored in this meals_provider.dart file,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 217.35,
          "end": 218.403,
          "en": "in this file here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 219.536,
          "end": 220.369,
          "en": "We're defining it here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 220.369,
          "end": 223.38,
          "en": "We are importing this file here in the tabs.dart file.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 223.38,
          "end": 225.42000000000002,
          "en": "Hence we can access this variable here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 225.42000000000002,
          "end": 228.453,
          "en": "and we're passing it as a value to watch.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 230.37,
          "end": 232.47,
          "en": "Now with that, we set up a listener",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 232.47,
          "end": 234.75,
          "en": "that will re-execute this build method",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 234.75,
          "end": 237.15,
          "en": "whenever this meals provider should change.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 237.15,
          "end": 239.76,
          "en": "So whenever the data in there should change,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 239.76,
          "end": 242.34,
          "en": "which this data here of course never does,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 242.34,
          "end": 246.39,
          "en": "but this will change later when we build other providers.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 246.39,
          "end": 249.33,
          "en": "Now nonetheless, with that we got this listener.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 249.33,
          "end": 252.84,
          "en": "And in addition, watch also returns the data",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 252.84,
          "end": 255.45,
          "en": "of the provider it watches.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 255.45,
          "end": 258.63,
          "en": "So here we also get our meals,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 258.63,
          "end": 260.403,
          "en": "which we can store in a variable.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 261.45,
          "end": 264.69,
          "en": "And you can see that it even infers the type correctly",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 264.69,
          "end": 267.33,
          "en": "because it is able to infer the type of data",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 267.33,
          "end": 269.883,
          "en": "we are returning here in our provider.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 270.99,
          "end": 274.02,
          "en": "So with that, we now get our meals, which we can use here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 274.02,
          "end": 278.01,
          "en": "to then filter those meals based on the filters we set.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 278.01,
          "end": 281.943,
          "en": "With that, if we save everything and force a restart,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 283.26,
          "end": 285.45,
          "en": "you get an error though,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 285.45,
          "end": 288.84000000000003,
          "en": "and you get an error because creating a provider",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 288.84000000000003,
          "end": 291.96,
          "en": "and extending these consumer classes",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 291.96,
          "end": 294.75,
          "en": "and then adding a watch like this is important,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 294.75,
          "end": 296.67,
          "en": "but it's not everything.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 296.67,
          "end": 298.77,
          "en": "Instead, there's another very important thing",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 298.77,
          "end": 301.53,
          "en": "you have to do in your Flutter app if you wanna use",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 104,
          "start": 301.53,
          "end": 303.72,
          "en": "this Riverpod package.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 105,
          "start": 303.72,
          "end": 306.72,
          "en": "You have to go to your main dart file,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 106,
          "start": 306.72,
          "end": 310.86,
          "en": "and there, where you're calling Run app,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 107,
          "start": 310.86,
          "end": 315.39,
          "en": "you have to wrap your app with another widget,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 108,
          "start": 315.39,
          "end": 319.59,
          "en": "another widget provided by the Riverpod package.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 109,
          "start": 319.59,
          "end": 321.69,
          "en": "Therefore here, we should also import",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 110,
          "start": 321.69,
          "end": 326.433,
          "en": "package:Flutter_Riverpod and then Flutter_riverpod.dart.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 111,
          "start": 327.57,
          "end": 331.03,
          "en": "And with that import added, we should wrap this here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 112,
          "start": 331.92,
          "end": 336.27,
          "en": "with another widget, which can also be set to const.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 113,
          "start": 336.27,
          "end": 339.943,
          "en": "And that widget would be the provider scope widget,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 114,
          "start": 339.943,
          "end": 342.603,
          "en": "which is a widget provided by Flutter_Riverpod.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 115,
          "start": 343.59000000000003,
          "end": 346.5,
          "en": "Provider Scope takes a child parameter,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 116,
          "start": 346.5,
          "end": 350.15999999999997,
          "en": "and the value of that parameter is our main entry widget,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 117,
          "start": 350.15999999999997,
          "end": 352.89,
          "en": "so the app widget in this case.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 118,
          "start": 352.89,
          "end": 355.74,
          "en": "But wrapping this app with provider scope",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 119,
          "start": 355.74,
          "end": 358.5,
          "en": "is important to unlock this",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 120,
          "start": 358.5,
          "end": 363.5,
          "en": "behind the scenes state management functionality in the end.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 121,
          "start": 363.51,
          "end": 366.15,
          "en": "And we are wrapping the entire app here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 122,
          "start": 366.15,
          "end": 369.03,
          "en": "so that all the widgets in the entire app",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 123,
          "start": 369.03,
          "end": 372.03,
          "en": "can use these Riverpod features.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 124,
          "start": 372.03,
          "end": 377.03,
          "en": "If you knew that only a certain nested part of your app",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 125,
          "start": 377.28,
          "end": 381.24,
          "en": "needed those features, it would be enough to wrap that part.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 126,
          "start": 381.24,
          "end": 383.94,
          "en": "But here I want to be able to use Riverpod",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 127,
          "start": 383.94,
          "end": 387.84,
          "en": "in the entire app, therefore I will wrap the entire app.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 128,
          "start": 387.84,
          "end": 391.38,
          "en": "And with that now, if you save this and force a reload,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 129,
          "start": 391.38,
          "end": 393.12,
          "en": "the error goes away.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 130,
          "start": 393.12,
          "end": 395.67,
          "en": "And now I can still see my meals here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 131,
          "start": 395.67,
          "end": 397.32,
          "en": "once I select a category.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 132,
          "start": 397.32,
          "end": 400.38,
          "en": "But now technically those meals are not fetched",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 133,
          "start": 400.38,
          "end": 404.46,
          "en": "by importing the dummy data file, at least not in a widget,",
          "zh": ""
